      "side": 1,
      "message": "I guess it depends where we draw the line between unit tests and other tests.\n\nMy view was that Rust unit tests were those using the `#[cfg(test)]` \u0026 `#[test]` framework to perform function-level testing. The tests themselves are typically written in the same file as their test targets and get cleanly packaged by Soong\u0027s `rust_test` to be run in a userspace framework on the Android host or even the build host. A great example of this are Jaewan\u0027s tests in `guest/pvmfw/src/device_assignment.rs`.\n\nThe code I\u0027m moving here is stand-alone (almost framework-like) code that expects the tested code as prebuilt binary and runs it, from the Android host, by spawning a VM. In particular, the `#[test]` functions are NOT actually testing host code (but guest code) and their scope is considerably higher than function-level.\n\nNote that we currently don\u0027t have actual function-level tests for `vmbase`. If we did, I fully agree it should live under `libs/libvmbase`. OTOH, the code in this CL feels closer to E2E testing.",
